{"name":"California Dreaming","hex":"#dec569","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dreaming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of dream"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of dreaming; a dream or reverie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreaming"}],"entries":[{"title":"California Dreaming (1979 film)","blocks":[{"text":"California Dreaming is a 1979 American comedy-drama film starring Glynnis O'Connor, Dennis Christopher, Seymour Cassel and Tanya Roberts and directed by John D. Hancock. The film explores the themes of growing up, finding love and self-knowledge, and reflects the contrast between life in industrial Chicago and the free Californian lifestyle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/California_Dreaming_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Dreaming_(1979_film)"},{"title":"California Dreaming (Rick Price and Jack Jones album)","blocks":[{"text":"California Dreaming is Rick's ninth studio album which is a 2017 collaborative album of covers by Australian singer-songwriters and musicians Rick Price and Jack Jones. The album sees Rick and Jack teaming together to re-imagine their favourite songs of the 1960s and 1970s California Sound era. The album was produced in Nashville by Sony executive Robert Rigby and is released through Sony Music Australia. The eponymous first single, by The Mamas & the Papas, was released in August. Songs from the album include hits by Neil Young and the Eagles. The album was released digitally and physically on 29 September and peaked at number 7 on the ARIA charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/California_Dreaming_by_Rick_Price_and_Jack_Jones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Dreaming_(Rick_Price_and_Jack_Jones_album)"},{"title":"California Dreamin'","blocks":[{"text":"\"California Dreamin'\" is a song written by John and Michelle Phillips. The best-known version is by the Mamas & the Papas, who released it as a single in December 1965."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/%22California_Dreamin%27%22_picture_sleeve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Dreamin'"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/California_Dreamin%27_Beach_Boys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/California_Dreamin%27_Beach_Boys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalifornia_Dreamin'_Beach_Boys.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikip